    {
      "id": "post-self-hosting",
      "workspaceId": "workspace-local",
      "title": "Self-Hosting — Coming Soon",
      "slug": "self-hosting",
      "bodyJson": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Coming soon.",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "bold"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " Managed self-hosting is on the roadmap. This page is a placeholder so we can describe what it will be."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "What we're building"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Today you run Tovu yourself: one binary, one folder, your machine. That will always work and will always be free. The coming service adds a managed path for people who want the ownership model without running a server."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "bulletList",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "One-click deploy of your Tovu folder to a host you control."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Automatic backups of the single site folder — database, uploads, themes, and plugins."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "A painless move from SQLite to Postgres when you outgrow a file, with no rewrite."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Bring-your-own-domain and TLS, handled for you."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "What won't change"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The important part: it stays "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "your",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " site. Managed hosting is a convenience layer over the same portable folder — export to a standalone binary and walk away at any time. No lock-in is the point, not a feature we can quietly remove."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "horizontalRule"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Want to be notified when self-hosting opens? That signup form is one of the pages still to build.",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "bodyFormat": "doc",
      "bodyHtml": null,
      "status": "published",
      "kind": "post",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "post-typography",
      "workspaceId": "workspace-local",
      "title": "Field Notes: The Weight of Type",
      "slug": "the-weight-of-type",
      "bodyJson": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Type has weight before it has meaning. Before a reader parses a single word, the shape of the page has already told them how to feel about it — formal or friendly, urgent or unhurried."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Three decisions that carry a page"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "orderedList",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Measure: the line length that keeps the eye from getting lost on the return sweep."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Rhythm: the vertical spacing that makes paragraphs feel like breathing, not stacking."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Contrast: the jump between a heading and its body that signals hierarchy without shouting."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The quiet defaults"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Most good typography is subtraction. A comfortable measure, one restrained typeface used at two or three sizes, and enough air. The failures are almost always additions — a second decorative face, a tighter leading to \"fit more,\" a heading that competes with its own body."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "blockquote",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The best typography disappears. You notice a page that is hard to read; you rarely notice one that is easy."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Which is the honest test for any theme: read a long paragraph on it, and see whether you finish."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "bodyFormat": "doc",
      "bodyHtml": null,
      "status": "published",
      "kind": "post",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "post-mornings",
      "workspaceId": "workspace-local",
      "title": "Slow Mornings",
      "slug": "slow-mornings",
      "bodyJson": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A slow morning is not an empty one. It is a morning with a deliberate order — a few small rituals that happen before the day starts asking for things."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A short list"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "bulletList",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Light before screens: open a window before you open a laptop."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "One warm thing, made slowly, with both hands."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Ten minutes of the day that belong to no one else."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "None of it is productive in the way the word usually means. That is the point. The morning is the one stretch of the day you can refuse to optimize."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "blockquote",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Begin gently, and the rest of the day has to negotiate with a calm person."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "bodyFormat": "doc",
      "bodyHtml": null,
      "status": "published",
      "kind": "post",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-07T00:00:00.000Z",
      "version": 1
    },
